---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | SoCal Trades"
  description="How SoCal Trades handles your data."
>
  <SiteHeader slot="header" />
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-10 text-lg text-gray-800">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-blue">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-base text-gray-600">
      This is a starting draft. Have it reviewed before launch.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-2xl font-bold text-brand-blue">What we collect</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      If you sign up for email updates, we store your email address to send you
      notices about new companies. You can unsubscribe at any time using the
      link in every email. If you claim a business profile, we store the email
      you verify with so you can manage that listing.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-2xl font-bold text-brand-blue">Google data</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Ratings, reviews, and open/closed status shown on profile pages come from
      the Google Places API and are fetched live when you view a page. We do not
      store Google review text or business hours.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-2xl font-bold text-brand-blue">Business listings</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Listing details such as company name, trade, city, and public contact
      information are shown so people can find and reach local trades companies.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-6 text-2xl font-bold text-brand-blue">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-3">
      Questions about your data? Email
      <a href="mailto:hello@socaltrades.net" class="text-brand-blue underline">
        hello@socaltrades.net
      </a>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <SiteFooter slot="footer" />
</BaseLayout>
